  "methodology": "Replay 45-second sessions on a virtual clock using the production detector in observe mode. Detection is any score at or above the frozen throttle threshold. The 25/15/35/25 signal weights are fixed; only the throttle threshold is selected on calibration traffic. Final test seeds and subject words are disjoint from calibration and the development pilot (seeds 1000-1019), which revealed invalid boundary probes. Final test labels never enter the detector. A campaign is one attack session, not three independent sessions. Detection timing is simulated arrival time, not a hardware latency measurement. The v2 sentiment update reuses the previously inspected v1 holdout as a fixed regression suite; these are not new unseen test sessions. Sarcasm regression examples are separate from this extraction-traffic benchmark.",
  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic traffic is narrower than real-world API behavior; shared generator families can overestimate generalization.",
